course: dictionary
lesson: 7979
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. The word reconcile is a good example. Most often it means to make friends again after a quarrel: «The two friends were reconciled» means they had an argument and then made peace.
explain: Reconcile can also mean to make two things agree. A checker might reconcile two sets of figures so they match, or show that two ideas can both be true. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Reconcile yourself to means to accept something unpleasant that you cannot change. To test your meaning, swap in a simpler idea and read the sentence again. If «make friends again» does not fit, try another meaning until the sentence makes sense.
fact: Reconcile means to make friends again after a quarrel, or to make two things agree.
fact: The noun is reconciliation, which means making peace after a quarrel.
fact: When people reconcile accounts, they check that the totals in two lists match.
fact: Reconcile yourself to something means accept it, even though you do not like it and cannot change it.
fact: In church teaching, Reconciliation means being brought back into friendship with God; in the Catholic Church, the sacrament of Reconciliation is confession.
exercise: «The two friends were reconciled after their quarrel.» What does reconciled mean here? | *Made friends again | Forgot each other's names | Went home early | Shouted at each other
exercise: Mum says, «I'll reconcile the accounts before we go shopping.» What is she going to do? | Tell a joke to the children | Buy new clothes for the trip | *Check that the totals match | Count the birds in the garden
exercise: Find and copy the noun that comes from reconcile. | friends | quarrel | *reconciliation | reconcile
test: Which phrase means to accept something unpleasant that you cannot change? | *Reconcile yourself to it | Reconcile the accounts | Reconcile the paint | Reconcile the stairs
test: Which is a good check for the meaning of reconcile in «The scientists tried to reconcile the two results»? | Ask if the results were loud | Ask if the scientists were tired | Ask if the results were made to agree or show they can both be true | *Ask if the results agree or can both be true
exam: Which word means making peace again after a quarrel? | wandered | *reconciled | guessed | scribbled
</br>
